---
// OPERATING EVIDENCE / HOW ASEPTACLEAN WORKS — built 2026-08-25 to
// docs/ASEPTACLEAN-CODEX-HOMEPAGE-BRIEF-V3-LEAN-SEVENSON.md §12.
//
// THIS ONE SECTION REPLACES THREE. §12 asks for a single concentrated credibility movement in
// place of the audited page's separate:
//   HandoffRecord         — the record band, a card on a flat navy field with no photograph
//   OperatorAccountability — the founder section, whose image column was an EMPTY BORDERED BOX
//   (no Project Notes section ever shipped, and none is invented here)
// Combined they ran 1,841px on desktop and 2,416px at 390px and asked the reader to accept the
// same idea — this company documents what it does — three times.
//
// THE EMPTY FOUNDER PHOTO BOX IS GONE. §12: "Do not render an empty bordered founder-photo box.
// That must disappear." No founder photograph exists in the repository and none is faked
// (AGENTS.md §0.3). What survives is the accountability statement, which is the part that was
// doing work; the slot that announced its own absence does not.
//
// NO FOUNDER BACKGROUND IS STATED HERE, deliberately, and that is why
// docs/21-CLAIMS-AND-COMPLIANCE-LAW.md §2.4's verbatim founder-authority clause does not appear.
// §2.4 binds "wherever the founder's background appears" — education, prior industry, prior
// technical experience. This section states a ROLE and an ACCOUNTABILITY, not a background:
// who reviews the scope, who stays responsible. §12 puts detailed credentials on About, and
// /about/ renders all four homepage.founderCredentials lines with legal.founderAuthorityLimit
// directly beneath them, which is where a reader who wants the background is sent.
//
// THE ARTIFACT IS INTEGRATED, NOT FLOATED. §12: "Do not place a small card in a huge empty navy
// field. The artifact must be integrated into a composition that works with or without a
// background photograph." It sits inside the copy column, on the same rhythm as the paragraphs
// above it, sharing the column with the heading and the link — not centred in dead space.
//
// SAMPLE STATUS IS EXPLICIT AND MANDATORY. "Sample · not a client record" is doc 27 §9.9's
// required label and AGENTS.md §0.3's hard line: this must never read as a real customer record.
// legal.documentationDisclaimer travels with it — doc 21 §6 requires that disclaimer "wherever
// the Property Handoff Record or any sample appears" — and is read from site data so it cannot
// drift.
//
// NO PROJECT NOTES ARE FABRICATED. Zero completed documented projects exist (doc 21 §6). When a
// real one does, §12 is where the page evolves toward real project evidence.
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import evidenceImage from "../assets/homepage/service-development-cleanup-asurnipal.jpg";
import { homepage, legal, site } from "@data/site";

// TEMPORARY DEVELOPMENT REFERENCE PHOTOGRAPH — NOT Aseptaclean work, not a client property, and
// not proof of a completed job. `[ATMOS]`-class under doc 21 §6's image rule: no crew, no
// technician, no vehicle, no equipment and no work in progress, so nothing in it implies
// Aseptaclean performed anything. It shows the KIND of property condition a handoff record gets
// written about, which is what puts the artifact beside it in context.
//   service-development-cleanup-asurnipal.jpg
//     Asurnipal — CC BY-SA 4.0
//     https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bregenz-Cluttered_interiors_(compulsive_hoarding)-dining_room-06ASD.jpg
// Replace with owner-shot photography before launch (docs/06-ASSET-MANIFEST.md §5). A real
// operator-at-work photograph is the highest-value replacement on the page.

const record = homepage.sampleRecord;
---

{/* Copy is FIRST IN THE DOM and placed into the right-hand column by grid. Source order is the
    reading order: the heading has to reach a screen reader before a decorative reference
    photograph and its development caption do. The photograph still opens the section visually at
    every width — left column on desktop, pulled to the top with `order` once the columns stack. */}
<section class="evidence" id="record" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
  <div class="evidence__inner">
    <div class="evidence__copy">
      <h2 id="evidence-title" class="ac-type-h2-home-feature">Clear work. Documented handoff.</h2>

      <p class="evidence__lede">
        The condition is reviewed, the work is written down, and the property is handed back with
        an account of what was decided and what was done.
      </p>
      <p class="evidence__accountability">
        {site.founder.name} is {site.founder.title}. He reviews the scope on every project and
        stays responsible for how the work is carried out — the same person on the assessment,
        the scope and the closeout.
      </p>

      <div class="record">
        <div class="record__head">
          <p class="record__title">Property Handoff Record</p>
          <p class="record__flag">Sample · not a client record</p>
        </div>

        <dl class="record__meta">
          <div><dt>Project</dt><dd>{record.projectId}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Decision-maker</dt><dd>{record.decisionMaker}</dd></div>
        </dl>

        <table class="record__table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Area</th>
              <th scope="col">Decision</th>
              <th scope="col">Note</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {record.rooms.map((room) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{room.area}</td>
                <td>{room.disposition}</td>
                <td>{room.note}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p class="record__note">{legal.documentationDisclaimer}</p>
      </div>

      <a class="evidence__link" href="/handoff-standard/">
        How a scope gets written <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <figure class="evidence__media">
      <Image
        src={evidenceImage}
        alt="Reference photograph of a dining room where accumulated household contents cover the table, sideboard and floor."
        widths={[520, 720, 960, 1240]}
        sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 46vw, 92vw"
        format="webp"
        quality={74}
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        Development reference photograph · not Aseptaclean project work · Asurnipal, Wikimedia
        Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .evidence {
    background: var(--ac-color-navy-900);
    padding-block: clamp(76px, 7.5vw, 112px);
  }

  .evidence__inner {
    display: grid;
    width: min(100% - 64px, 1320px);
    align-items: start;
    margin-inline: auto;
    gap: 48px 72px;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.12fr);
  }

  /* Explicit placement puts the photograph back in the LEFT column while staying second in the
     DOM. Sticky so it stays with the artifact through the taller copy column instead of running
     out at the top of a long scroll — it is the section's largest element, which is what keeps
     this a photographic moment rather than a document on a navy background. */
  .evidence__media {
    position: sticky;
    top: 96px;
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 1;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .evidence__copy {
    grid-column: 2;
    grid-row: 1;
  }

  .evidence__media :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    background: var(--ac-color-navy-950);
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 54%;
  }

  .evidence__media figcaption {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 52%);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* V3 §23: 36–42px, set on the token so the size still resolves through the role class
     (AGENTS.md §6 law 1). */
  .evidence__copy {
    --ac-text-h2-home-feature: 2.5rem;
  }

  .evidence__copy h2 {
    max-width: 16ch;
    color: var(--ac-color-paper);
  }

  .evidence__lede {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    max-width: 48ch;
    color: #ccd9e8;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.62;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .evidence__accountability {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    max-width: 48ch;
    color: #a9bdd4;
    line-height: 1.66;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* The artifact is drawn as a document: square edges, a ruled register, one accent rule at the
     top. Not a rounded card, and not a floating panel — it is the next block in the column. */
  .record {
    border-top: 3px solid var(--ac-color-blue-on-navy);
    margin-top: 32px;
    background: var(--ac-color-paper);
    padding: 22px 24px 24px;
  }

  .record__head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 6px 18px;
  }

  .record__title {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ac-color-navy-900);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* doc 27 §9.9's REQUIRED label. Never remove it, never soften it, and never let it become
     less legible than the record it labels. */
  .record__flag {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ac-color-review);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .record__meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    gap: 4px 28px;
  }

  .record__meta > div {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .record__meta dt {
    color: var(--ac-color-ink-400);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .record__meta dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ac-color-navy-900);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .record__table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 16px;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .record__table th {
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ac-color-navy-800);
    padding: 0 14px 8px 0;
    color: var(--ac-color-navy-900);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .record__table td {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ac-color-line);
    padding: 11px 14px 11px 0;
    color: var(--ac-color-ink-600);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .record__table td:first-child {
    color: var(--ac-color-navy-900);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .record__table th:last-child,
  .record__table td:last-child {
    padding-right: 0;
  }

  .record__note {
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    color: var(--ac-color-ink-600);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .evidence__link {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 26px;
    color: var(--ac-color-paper);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-underline-offset: 5px;
  }

  .evidence__link:hover {
    color: var(--ac-color-blue-pale);
  }

  .evidence__link:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--ac-color-paper);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 64rem) {
    .evidence__inner {
      width: min(100% - 52px, 1320px);
      gap: 40px 44px;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    }

    .evidence__copy {
      --ac-text-h2-home-feature: 2.25rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 50rem) {
    /* Flex, not a one-column grid: the explicit grid-column/grid-row placement above would put
       both children in the same cell and overlap them. `order` restores the photograph to the
       top while the DOM keeps copy first. */
    .evidence__inner {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 32px;
    }

    .evidence__media {
      position: static;
      order: -1;
    }

    .evidence__media :global(img) {
      aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
    }

    .evidence__copy h2 {
      max-width: 20ch;
    }

    .evidence__lede,
    .evidence__accountability {
      max-width: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .evidence {
      padding-block: 60px;
    }

    .evidence__inner {
      width: calc(100% - 40px);
    }

    .evidence__copy {
      --ac-text-h2-home-feature: 2rem;
    }

    .record {
      padding: 20px 18px 22px;
    }

    /* The three-column record table is the one element that cannot survive a 390px viewport as a
       table — the Note column collapses to two words a line. Below 40rem each row becomes a
       labelled block, which keeps the same reading order and the same <table> semantics for
       assistive technology. */
    .record__table thead {
      position: absolute;
      overflow: hidden;
      width: 1px;
      height: 1px;
      clip-path: inset(50%);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .record__table tr {
      display: block;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ac-color-line);
      padding-block: 12px;
    }

    .record__table tr:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .record__table td {
      display: block;
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .record__table td:first-child {
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
    }

    .record__table td:nth-child(2) {
      margin-top: 2px;
      color: var(--ac-color-navy-800);
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .record__table td:last-child {
      margin-top: 4px;
    }
  }

  /* NARROWEST BAND ONLY, 2026-08-26. At 320px "Clear work. Documented handoff." broke to three
     lines with "handoff." alone on the last one — the one-word final line doc 30 §8.3 rejects.
     §8.3's fix order was worked through in sequence: the container is already the section's own
     `calc(100% - 40px)` and widening it cannot help (the phrase needs 320px at 32px type, which
     is the whole viewport); there is no grid allocation to change at one column; `max-width:
     20ch` is not the binding constraint; and the measure is set by the phrase itself. That
     exhausts everything above "font size only when necessary", so the size steps — measured,
     not guessed: 29px still wraps to three lines, 28px is the largest value that keeps
     "Documented handoff." whole in the 280px available.
     Set on the token, never on the heading (AGENTS.md §6 law 1) — the size still resolves
     through .ac-type-h2-home-feature. 22.5rem matches the hero's existing narrow step. */
  @media (max-width: 22.5rem) {
    .evidence__copy {
      --ac-text-h2-home-feature: 1.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
